document {
    type: A4
    margin: 4
}

elem header {
    name,
    tagline,
    contact,
}

elem separator {
    title,
}

elem skills {
    languages,
    systems,
    tools,
}

elem project {
    title,
    stack,
    link,
    content,
}

elem entry {
    company,
    role,
    date,
    content,
}

elem education {
    institution,
    location,
    degree,
    date,
    content,
}

elem colophon {
    text,
}

layout header {
    <> name
    <> tagline
    <> contact

    name: xl
    tagline: sm
    contact: sm
}

layout separator {
    title
    ---

    title: md
}

layout skills {
    languages
    systems
    tools

    languages: sm
    systems: sm
    tools: sm
}

layout project {
    < title | > link
    stack
    content

    title: sm
    link: sm
    stack: sm
    content: sm
}

layout entry {
    < role | > date
    company
    content

    company: sm
    date: sm
    role: sm
    content: sm
}

layout education {
    < institution | > date
    degree
    content

    institution: sm
    location: sm
    degree: sm
    date: sm
    content: sm
}

layout colophon {
    <> text

    text: sm
}

@header {
    name: **Erik Scholtz**
    tagline: Systems engineer building compilers, firmware and developer tools
    contact: [erikscholtz23@gmail.com](mailto:erikscholtz23@gmail.com) | [linkedin.com/in/erikscholtz](https://linkedin.com/in/erikscholtz) | [github.com/erscholtz](https://github.com/erscholtz)
}

@separator {
    title: **EXPERIENCE**
}

@entry {
    company: Deloitte · Toronto, ON
    role: **Infrastructure Engineer**
    date: *September 2025 – Present*

    - Building an LLM agent tool to map client data onto existing apps: normalizes JSON, XLSX and SQLite sources into intermediate JSON schemas, proposes candidate mappings with casting options, and verifies them through a decision model, schema dry runs and synthetic data before human review.
    - Applied constraint-solving techniques to CI resource scheduling, reducing queue times by 20% under shared compute constraints.
}

@entry {
    company: Syncademia AI · Waterloo, ON
    role: **Infrastructure Engineer**
    date: *January 2025 – August 2025*

    - Built a streaming document ingestion pipeline with backpressure handling to process 1000+ page inputs without exceeding memory limits.
    - Reduced dependency surface area by 40% through targeted library audit and replacement, simplifying runtime behavior and eliminating classes of failure.
}

@entry {
    company: Deloitte · Toronto, ON
    role: **Software Engineering Co-op**
    date: *May 2024 – September 2024*

    - Developed a telemetry tool to analyze system logs and visualize object dependencies, adopted by multiple enterprise teams for debugging.
}

@separator {
    title: **PROJECTS**
}

@project {
    title: **pyrus: Typesetting language and compiler**
    stack: `Rust · Pratt Parsing · HIR · Text Shaping · PDF`
    link: [github](https://github.com/erscholtz/pyrus)

    - Built a compiler from lexer to parser, HIR, layout and PDF output, with shaping through harfrust and PDF generation through krilla. It compiled this page.
    - Implemented a recursive descent parser with Pratt-style operator precedence and string interpolation.
}

@project {
    title: **harnessd: Autocomplete daemon**
    stack: `Rust · Tokio · tree-sitter · SQLite · JSON-RPC`
    link: [github](https://github.com/erscholtz/harnessd)

    - Built a daemon with local IPC, lockfile-based single-instance control and graceful shutdown, serving editor and CLI requests over JSON-RPC 2.0.
    - Designed a rusqlite proposal cache keyed by file path, byte range and content hash, with invalidation guards keeping completions coherent with source changes.
    - Used tree-sitter to map cursor offsets to AST regions and precompute suggestions from TODO/FIXME anchors across multiple languages.
}

@project {
    title: **UEFI Secure Boot CVE Replication**
    stack: `C · EDK-II · QEMU · UEFI Secure Boot`
    link: [github](https://github.com/erscholtz/uefi-cve-replication)

    - Replicated `CVE-2022-21894` (Baton Drop) in QEMU to analyze the Secure Boot bypass.
    - Proposed an EDK-II proof-of-concept patch using a monotonic counter with EFI signing timestamps to prevent rollback attacks.
}

@separator {
    title: **SKILLS**
}

@skills {
    languages: **Languages:** `Rust, C, Python`
    systems: **Systems:** `UEFI/EDK-II, QEMU, IPC, JSON-RPC, SQLite`
    tools: **Tools:** `Cargo, Make, KBuild, Git`
}

